                  %a{:href => "#automorphisms"} Automorphisms
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#NImagesOf1FunctorsBetweenGroupoids"} Of functors between groupoids
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The generalization of the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ViaEpiMonoFactorization
            By epi/mono factorization in an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n-connected%2C+n-truncated%29+factorization+system"} (n-connected, n-truncated) factorization system
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} orthogonal factorization system
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi Epi
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Mono
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  Epi(\mathbf{H}), Mono(\mathbf{H})
                  \\big)
                  \\,\subset\,
                  Mor(\mathbf{H}) \times Mor(\mathbf{H})
          %p
            whose left class consists of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (-1)-connected
            morphisms, the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-effective epimorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (-1)-truncated morphisms
            morphisms, hence the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-monomorphisms
          %p
            So given a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            with epi-mono factorization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f : X \to im_1(f) \hookrightarrow Y
                  \\,,
          %p
            we may call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_1(f) \hookrightarrow Y
            the
            %strong image
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %h3#ViaColimitOfCechNerve As the ∞-colimit of the kernel ∞-groupoid
          %p
            In a sufficiently well-behaved 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"}> category
            , the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coimage"} (co)image
            of a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            may be defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \times_Y X \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} X \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} im(f)
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimiting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphism"} parallel morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
          %p
            In an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            the 1-image is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            not just of these two morphisms, but of the full “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-kernel”, namely of the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  X \times_Y X \times_Y X
                  \\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}}
                  X \times_Y X \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} X \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} im(f)
                  \\,.
          %p (Here all degeneracy maps are notionally suppressed.)
          %p
            To see that this gives the same notion of image as given by the epi-mono factorization as discussed
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ViaEpiMonoFactorization"} above
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                  %mi im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} im(f) \hookrightarrow Y
            be such a factorization. Then using (by the discussion at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "n-truncated+object+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category#RecursiveDefinition"} truncated morphism – Recursive characterization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism
            is its domain, we find a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            squares of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %mi im
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi im
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mi im
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi im
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \times_{im(f)} X &amp;\to &amp; X &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to} &amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; im(f) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; im(f)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; im(f) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; Y
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            which shows, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi im
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_{Y} X \simeq X \times_{im(f)} X
            and hence that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y
            is equivalently that of the effective epimorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{f}{\to} im(f)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud-Rezk-Lurie+axioms"} Giraud-Rezk-Lurie axioms
            satisfied by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
            is that morphism itself. Therefore the 1-image defined this way coincides with the one defined by the epi/mono factorization.
          %h3#tower_of_images
            Tower of
            = succeed "-images" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            More generally for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            a morphism we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower"} tower
            of
            = succeed "-images" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \simeq im_\infty(f) \to \cdots \to im_2(f) \to im_1(f) \to im_0(f) \simeq Y
          %p
            factoring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            the factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi im
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to im_{n+2}(f) \to Y
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n-connected%2C+n-truncated%29+factorization+system"} (n-connected, n-truncated) factorization system
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            This is the relative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+system"} Postnikov system
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#SyntaxInHomotopyTypeTheory Syntax in homotopy type theory
          %p
            Let the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            of 1-images in this theory.
          #SyntaxOfInfinityImage.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p If
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \colon A
                    \\;\vdash\;
                    f(a) \,\colon\, B
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \xrightarrow{f} B
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}/B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Type
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (b:B)
                    \\;\;
                    \\vdash
                    \\;\;
                    \\Big[
                    (a \colon A)
                    \\times
                    \\big(b = f(a) \big)
                    \\Big]_0
                    \\,\colon\,
                    Type
                    \\,,
          %p Here
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a \colon A) \times C_a
                denotes the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+pair+type"} dependent pair type
            %li
              %p
                “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =
                ” denotes the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification+type"} identification type
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-]_0
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bracket+type"} bracket type
                (which is constructible in homotopy type theory either as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
                as described at
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncation+modality"} n-truncation modality
                or using the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
                and a resizing rule to obtain a
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{M}
              be a suitable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presenting
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (b \colon B)
                    ,\,
                    (a \colon A)
                    \\;\;\vdash\;\;
                    \\big(
                    b = f(a)
                    \\big)
                    \\,:\, Type
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{M}
              a is the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A
              (see
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              for more details):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi I
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi id
                                  %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde A &amp;\to&amp; B^{I}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A \times B &amp;\stackrel{(f,id_B)}{\to}&amp; B \times B
                    }.
            %p
              Here all objects now denote
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
              representatives of the given objects in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
              out of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A \to A \times B \to B
              here is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              of the original
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{f}{\to} B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A \to A \times B
              is a fibration resolution of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{(id_A,f)}{\to} A \times B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{M}/(A \times B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b = f(a))
              as an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \times B)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            %p
              Now the interpretation of the sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{a:A}
              is simply that we forget the map to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              (or equivalently compose with the projection
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times B\to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A
              as an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{M}/B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              itself.
            %p
              Finally, the interpretation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bracket+type"} bracket type
              of this is precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (-1)-truncation
              of this morphism, which by the discussion there is its 1-image
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi im
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im_1(\tilde A \to B)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            By additionally forgetting the remaining map to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          #NonDependentSyntax.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              In the above situation, the 1-image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              itself, is the semantics of the non-dependent type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} [
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vdash \;
                    \\Big(\Big(
                    \\sum_{b:B}\Big[\sum_{a:A} (b = f(a))\Big]
                    \\Big)
                    \: Type\Big).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The bracket type of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+some+types"} propositions as some types
              version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SyntaxOfInfinityImage"}
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi hProp
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (b:B) \; \vdash \;
                    \\left(\exists a:A . (b = f(a))
                    \\;:\; hProp\right).
            %p
              The dependent sum
              %em of
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
              is then the propositions-as-some-types version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehension+rule"} comprehension rule
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{b \in B | \phi(b)\}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonDependentSyntax"}
              may be written as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    b \in B \,|\, \exists a \in A . (b = f(a))
                    \\right\}
            %p
              which is manifestly the naive definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
          %h3#compatibility_with_limits Compatibility with limits
          #nImagePreservesProducts.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              In an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "-image" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-images:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
